# udev rules for clackd — grant the active session unprivileged access
# to VIA-capable keyboards over hidraw.
#
# Install location:
#   /etc/udev/rules.d/60-clackd-via.rules
#
# After installing (or editing) this file:
#   sudo udevadm control --reload
#   sudo udevadm trigger
#
# # Why this is needed
#
# `clackd` runs as a regular user (CLAUDE.md §6). For it to read and
# write /dev/hidrawX nodes without CAP_SYS_RAWIO, udev must grant the
# active login session an ACL on the node. The `TAG+="uaccess"` mark is
# what triggers that ACL — see systemd-logind(8) and udev(7).
#
# # Why per-device rules
#
# VIA is a firmware feature, not a vendor or USB-class identifier. The
# kernel exposes USB VID/PID to udev but does NOT expose HID Usage Page
# (which is what distinguishes VIA endpoints — page 0xFF60). Daemon
# itself probes the descriptor at attach time, but udev can only filter
# coarsely.
#
# # Recommended approach
#
# Add one line per keyboard you want clackd to manage. The VID/PID can
# be read from `lsusb` or from `udevadm info /dev/hidrawN`.
#
# Examples (uncomment and adjust the IDs to match your hardware):
#
#   # Drop ALT — vid 04d8 pid eed3
#   #SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="04d8", ATTRS{idProduct}=="eed3", TAG+="uaccess"
#
#   # Keychron K2 V2 — vid 3434 pid 0151
#   #SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3434", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0151", TAG+="uaccess"
#
#   # Epomaker EK68 / Zuoya GMK67 (non-VIA, driver=gmk67) — vid 05ac pid 024f
#   #SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="05ac", ATTRS{idProduct}=="024f", TAG+="uaccess"
#
#   # Generic placeholder
#   #SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="XXXX", ATTRS{idProduct}=="YYYY", TAG+="uaccess"
#
# # Permissive alternative (NOT recommended)
#
# If you want every hidraw node to be session-accessible — handy for
# discovery but loose on security. The daemon will still refuse to
# attach to non-VIA devices thanks to its Usage Page probe, but other
# applications on the session will also be able to open mice, joysticks, etc.

SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", TAG+="uaccess"

